<br/>When fully raid buffed with consumables, a bear wearing the above set will achieve the following tank metrics:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">57,971 HP (<i>far</i> more than any other tank spec)</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">36,793 armor</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">58.6% avoidance</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">11,700 TPS</div></li></ul>The ability to access such a sky-high effective health pool (EHP) while wearing primarily melee DPS gear makes Feral Druids phenomenal off-tanks in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a>, particularly on encounters like <b>Northrend Beasts</b> where the off-tank may spend a significant fraction of the encounter DPSing in their tank gear.<br/>
<br/>Note that the displayed configuration is well over the Hit cap for either faction (8% Hit for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>
<span class="q10">Horde</span> bears, 7% Hit for <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span>
<span class="q3">Alliance</span> bears with the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=6562/heroic-presence">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Presence</span></a> buff). This is simply a consequence of the best itemized leather tanking gear in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a> being overloaded in Hit Rating. As a result, even with zero value given to the Hit Rating stat during gear optimizations, BiS setups in Phase 3 will always end up far above the cap.<br/>
<br/>Also note that the above BiS configuration intentionally foregoes the 4-piece Tier 9 set bonus in favor of higher value off-pieces. Simulation comparisons indicate that the 30 additional Stamina on <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47004/cuirass-of-calamitous-fate">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_14.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cuirass of Calamitous Fate</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46975/leggings-of-the-broken-beast">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_leather_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leggings of the Broken Beast</span></a> relative to their Tier 9 counterparts (due to the extra gem socket on the off-pieces) outweighs the value of higher <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=22812/barkskin">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_stoneclawtotem.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Barkskin</span></a> uptime from the 4-piece bonus.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="survival">Survival Set</h3>While the above gear set is capable of surviving all of the raid content in Phase 3, a select few tanking assignments in <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> are known to be particularly punishing for tank survival even when the content is on farm. In <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4722/trial-of-the-crusader">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Crusader</span></a>, the most notable examples of this are main tanking <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34796/gormok-the-impaler">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Gormok the Impaler</span></a> through several <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66331/impale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_throw.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Impale</span></a> stacks without a tank swap, or off-tanking <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34607/nerubian-burrower">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Nerubian Burrower</span></a> adds on the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a> encounter. In <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a>, Hard Mode <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32867/steelbreaker">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Steelbreaker</span></a> and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a> continue to fall in this category even when decked out in Phase 3 gear. For this reason, a second "maximum survival" gear set is presented below, with the goal of minimizing the risk of a tank death on these few encounters:<br/>
