<br/>Compared to the balanced configuration, the pure survival setup above swaps in <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45245/shoulderpads-of-the-intruder">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shoulder_51.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shoulderpads of the Intruder</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47549/magnis-resolution">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Magni's Resolution</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47155/bracers-of-dark-determination">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_23b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bracers of Dark Determination</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49489/signified-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signified Ring of Binding</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48523/relentless-gladiators-greatstaff">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_105.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relentless Gladiator's Greatstaff</span></a>, and the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41380/austere-earthsiege-diamond">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_shadowspirit_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Austere Earthsiege Diamond</span></a> meta gem in order to access even higher Stamina levels. With these swaps in place, Feral tanks can achieve a whopping <b>65,000 HP</b> in a raid setting, making them effectively immortal against any WotLK raid boss.<br/>
<br/>Note that both of the above BiS setups include the Engineering-exclusive enchants <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=63770/reticulated-armor-webbing">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reticulated Armor Webbing</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67839/mind-amplification-dish">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mind Amplification Dish</span></a>. As mentioned in our <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/druid/feral/tank-overview-pve#best-professions">class overview guide</a>, <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=202/engineering">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> is such an insanely overpowered profession for PvE that it is assumed that any competitive Feral tank player will have it. In contrast, your second profession choice has hardly any impact in WotLK since all crafting professions provide very comparable PvE benefits, so no other profession-exclusive gear augmentations are assumed.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="anubarak-nr">Anub'arak Nature Resistance Set</h3>Finally, this guide also includes a third specialized gear set optimized for main tanking <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a>. This tanking role will often be performed by Feral Druids since Warrior and Paladin tanks are much more effective at handling the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34607/nerubian-burrower">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Nerubian Burrower</span></a> adds, and has some unique gearing considerations relative to any other encounter. On one hand, the boss himself (unlike the adds) is not very threatening even on 25-man Heroic difficulty, and has very limited burst damage potential even during <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66012/freezing-slash">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostblast.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Freezing Slash</span></a> stuns due to his slow swing timer. Conversely, running <i>too much</i> HP is actively detrimental during Phase 3 of the encounter due to the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66118/leeching-swarm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_insectswarm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leeching Swarm</span></a> mechanic, which continuously heals the boss based on the tank's current HP. Since the main tank still needs to be topped off before each <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66012/freezing-slash">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostblast.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Freezing Slash</span></a>, they will be by far the largest contributor to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66118/leeching-swarm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_insectswarm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leeching Swarm</span></a> healing across the raid, which can considerably slow down the Phase 3 burn.<br/>
<br/>There are two efficient strategies for mitigating <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66118/leeching-swarm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_insectswarm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leeching Swarm</span></a> healing as the main tank:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Intentionally dropping some Stamina and substituting other survival stats like Armor and Dodge in its place. This is most efficiently done via trinket and gem swaps.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">While standard damage reduction effects like <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=22812/barkskin">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_stoneclawtotem.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Barkskin</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=53530/divine-guardian">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_powerwordbarrier.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Divine Guardian</span></a> have no effect on <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66118/leeching-swarm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_insectswarm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leeching Swarm</span></a>, partial resists <i>do</i> reduce the damage (and healing) done by the ability, making Nature Resistance (NR) an extremely high value stat for the main tank role.</div></li></ol>The gear set shown below incorporates both of these strategies self-consistently:<br/>
<div style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<div class="gear-planner" data-data-env-key="wrath" data-faction="1" data-player-class="druid" data-player-gender="1" data-player-level="80" data-player-race="night-elf" data-player-race-id="4" id="markup-gear-planner-calc-2">
