<div class="gear-planner-modelviewer" data-currently-visible="true"></div></div></div></div>
<br/>When combined with <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44939/lesser-flask-of-resistance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_potion_118.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lesser Flask of Resistance</span></a> and a Nature Resistance raid buff (either <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=58749/nature-resistance-totem">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_natureresistancetotem.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nature Resistance Totem</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=49071/aspect-of-the-wild">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_protectionformnature.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Aspect of the Wild</span></a>), this setup can reach 323 NR, which corresponds to 38.8% mitigation of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66118/leeching-swarm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_insectswarm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leeching Swarm</span></a> healing. Leatherworkers can further boost this to 393 NR (43.5% mitigation) via <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=57699/fur-lining-nature-resist">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fur Lining - Nature Resist</span></a>. In order, the most efficient NR swaps in the setup are <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44138/arcanum-of-toxic-warding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_brewpoison.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of Toxic Warding</span></a>, followed by the 25-man and 10-man <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=10184/onyxia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Onyxia</span></a> rings (<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49489/signified-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signified Ring of Binding</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49309/runed-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runed Ring of Binding</span></a>), followed by <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44494/enchant-cloak-superior-nature-resistance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulagood_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Cloak - Superior Nature Resistance</span></a>. On top of these, <a class="q2 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=29487/nature-armor-kit">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_spiritarmor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nature Armor Kit</span></a>, <a class="q2 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=29187/inscription-of-endurance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_shieldmastery.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscription of Endurance</span></a>, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=22459/void-sphere">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_voidsphere.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Void Sphere</span></a>
<span class="q4">s</span> are further optional min-max optimizations for even more NR, but may be impractical to swap in for just a single boss.<br/>
<br/>Additionally, this setup drops about 11,000 HP relative to the first balanced set presented above by using <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47735/glyph-of-indomitability">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Indomitability</span></a> instead of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a>, and by swapping in several hybrid <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40130/shifting-dreadstone">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_40.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shifting Dreadstone</span></a> gems in place of pure Stamina gems. Doing so still leaves you with almost 47,000 raid buffed HP, which is more than sufficient to comfortably main tank <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a>, but will dramatically lower your total healing on the boss in Phase 3. For early progression kills, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40257/defenders-code">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_trinket_naxxramas05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Defender's Code</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44253/darkmoon-card-greatness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tarotgreatness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmoon Card: Greatness</span></a> can be used in place of <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> Stamina trinkets to the same effect.<br/>
<br/>Importantly, both of these optimizations (adding Nature Resistance and deliberately lowering Stamina) should <i>only</i> be performed by the main tank. If you are assigned to off-tank the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34607/nerubian-burrower">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Nerubian Burrower</span></a> adds instead, then you should stick with the maximum survival setup shown above. These adds have insanely high burst damage potential, so optimizing for personal survivability is significantly more important than limiting <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66118/leeching-swarm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_insectswarm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leeching Swarm</span></a> healing in this role.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Triumph for Feral Druid Tank Phase 3</h3>The only <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a> reward in the BiS gear setups shown above is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47735/glyph-of-indomitability">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Indomitability</span></a>, which is worse than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a> from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> for general tanking value but is the optimal choice for main tanking <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a> due to its lack of Stamina.  The other rewards are all outclassed by 258 Item Level drops from 25-man Heroic bosses, but can serve as solid intermediate upgrades while you are waiting for the BiS option to drop. In particular, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47731/clutch-of-fortification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_50naxxramas.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Clutch of Fortification</span></a> provides a hefty survivability increase over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45112/the-leviathans-coil">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_71.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Leviathan's Coil</span></a> from Phase 2, and is worth the investment unless you get lucky with BiS ring drops early in the phase. Once you have purchased <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47735/glyph-of-indomitability">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Indomitability</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47731/clutch-of-fortification">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_50naxxramas.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Clutch of Fortification</span></a>, it is recommended to save up 120 Emblems so that you can purchase the 245 Item Level version of the Tier 9 helm and gloves as soon as possible after obtaining 2x <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47242/trophy-of-the-crusade">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trophy_argent.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Trophy of the Crusade</span></a> from raids. Note that it is <i>not</i> recommended to spend any of your Emblems on the 232 Item Level ("of Conquest") versions of the Tier 9 pieces, as these are often downgrades from Tier 8 for tanking and will delay you from obtaining the more impactful 245 pieces.<br/>
