<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="rings">Rings for Feral Druid Tank Phase 3</h3>There are several strong ring options to choose from in Phase 3, any of which can be optimal depending on the encounter and your tanking role. For general tanking value, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47955/loop-of-the-twin-valkyr">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Loop of the Twin Val'kyr</span></a> + <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47075/ring-of-callous-aggression">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_65.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of Callous Aggression</span></a> is the optimal ring pairing for balanced gear sets, supplying a healthy mix of EHP, avoidance, and Threat stats. When gearing for maximum survivability, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49489/signified-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signified Ring of Binding</span></a> off <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=10184/onyxia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Onyxia</span></a> (25) is an efficient EHP swap that should be used in place of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47075/ring-of-callous-aggression">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_65.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of Callous Aggression</span></a>. If you are main tanking <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a>, then the 10-man version of the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=10184/onyxia">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Onyxia</span></a> ring can also be substituted in place of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47955/loop-of-the-twin-valkyr">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_59.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Loop of the Twin Val'kyr</span></a>, providing you with 55 Nature Resistance for mitigating <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66118/leeching-swarm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_insectswarm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leeching Swarm</span></a> healing just from your ring slots.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Ring Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59636/enchant-ring-stamina">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Ring - Stamina</span></a>, requires <a class="icontiny" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/skill=333/enchanting">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engraving.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchanting</span></a>. <br/>Only Enchanters may apply ring enchants on their own rings.<div class="pad"></div>
