<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Feral Druid Tank Phase 3</h3>Phase 3 introduces multiple new tanking trinkets for bears to choose from, and similar to the ring slot, the optimal choice can vary based on the encounter and tanking role. The two overall highest value trinket options are, unsurprisingly, the ones with the highest item level: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47451/juggernauts-vitality">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Juggernaut's Vitality</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47464/deaths-choice">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Choice</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47131/deaths-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Verdict</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>If you tanked on your Feral Druid during TBC Classic, then you should already be familiar with the power of "Last Stand trinkets" like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=32501/shadowmoon-insignia">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_shadowsongamethyst_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadowmoon Insignia</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=34428/steely-naaru-sliver">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Steely Naaru Sliver</span></a>, which are extremely efficient for tank survival because they collapse a huge amount of effective Stamina into an on-use effect that you can activate precisely when you need the extra health, either when anticipating a "tank buster" ability from a raid boss or when reacting to bad RNG such as a long sequence of incoming hits without a dodge. While similar trinkets have also existed in WotLK in prior phases, they were unfortunately under-tuned and could not compete with passive Stamina trinkets. With <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> in Phase 3, we finally have a competitive Last Stand trinket at our disposal again. Just the passive Stamina on it alone makes it the optimal choice for survivability, so its associated <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67753/fortitude">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_mindvision.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fortitude</span></a> cooldown makes it even better!<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47131/deaths-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Verdict</span></a> is the more balanced counterpart to the raw survivability from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a>, and serves the same function as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44253/darkmoon-card-greatness">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_tarotgreatness.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmoon Card: Greatness</span></a> in Phase 1 by providing a mixture of Armor, Dodge, and Crit via its high uptime <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67772/paragon">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_proclaimchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Paragon</span></a> proc. However, this trinket will be extremely contested in most raid groups, so it will be difficult to justify taking it unless you are an off-tank who will also get DPS value from it in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a>. Note that for pure survivability, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a> from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> still outperforms <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47131/deaths-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Verdict</span></a>, and should be swapped in when tanking mobs with high burst damage potential such as <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a> or <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34607/nerubian-burrower">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Nerubian Burrower</span></a> adds.<br/>
<br/>As mentioned at the start of this guide, a third new tanking trinket, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47735/glyph-of-indomitability">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Indomitability</span></a>, is also introduced in Phase 3 as an <a class="icontiny q1" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=301/emblem-of-triumph">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_summonchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Triumph</span></span></a> reward. While this trinket is worse for general survivability than both <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47088/satrinas-impeding-scarab">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satrina's Impeding Scarab</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a>, it is situationally BiS when main tanking <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=34564/anubarak">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Anub'arak</span></a> because it provides its defensive benefits in the form of Armor and Dodge rather than Stamina, making it an optimal choice on this encounter for staying tanky while minimizing your <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=66118/leeching-swarm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_insectswarm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leeching Swarm</span></a> healing on the boss.<br/>
<br/>Finally, it is worth calling attention to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47216/the-black-heart">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_bloodstone_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Black Heart</span></a>, an introductory tank trinket from the new 5-man <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4723/trial-of-the-champion">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Trial of the Champion</span></a> dungeon. Despite its low item level, this trinket is actually competitive with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a> for survival value, and outperforms both <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47735/glyph-of-indomitability">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Indomitability</span></a> and the Phase 2 BiS trinket <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46021/royal-seal-of-king-llane">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_crown_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Royal Seal of King Llane</span></a>! In addition to its respectable passive Stamina, the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67631/aegis">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/classic_spell_holy_blessingofprotection.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Aegis</span></a> buff from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47216/the-black-heart">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_bloodstone_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">The Black Heart</span></a> has a very high proc rate from incoming attacks and will be applied almost immediately off cooldown, making it a reliable source of temporary damage reduction at the start of a boss pull.<div class="pad"></div>
