<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons and Idols for Feral Druid Tank Phase 3</h2>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="weapons-for-feral-druid-tank-phase-3">Weapons for Feral Druid Tank Phase 3</h4>The top weapon option for the majority of main tanking and off-tanking roles in Phase 3 encounters will be the 258 Item Level staff off the Twin Val'kyr, but the Season 7 Arena weapon <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48523/relentless-gladiators-greatstaff">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_105.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relentless Gladiator's Greatstaff</span></a> is an efficient survivability swap for scenarios where you want to beef up as much as possible.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64579/enchant-weapon-blood-draining">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_note_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Blood Draining</span></a>
<br/>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> introduced a brand new type of weapon enchant for tanks with a novel mechanism of action. When the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64571/blood-draining">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_bloodstone_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Draining</span></a> aura from this enchant is active, your Threat generating abilities will apply a new stack of the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64568/blood-reserve">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_bloodstone_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Reserve</span></a> buff once every 10 seconds, up to a maximum of 5 stacks. Whenever you fall below 35% health, the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64569/blood-reserve">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_resistmagic.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Reserve</span></a> heal will automatically kick in and consume your accumulated stacks, providing an average of 400 instant healing per stack. Simulations of tank survival on hard hitting bosses like <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a> indicate that Blood Draining is 2.7 times more effective at preventing tank deaths than the Mongoose enchant that was optimal in Phase 1.<div class="pad"></div>
