<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="idols-for-feral-druid-tank-phase-3">Idols for Feral Druid Tank Phase 3</h4>In Phase 3, Feral tanks will continue to use <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45509/idol-of-the-corruptor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Corruptor</span></a> as the optimal choice for boss encounters, and this Idol will fortunately be much easier to attain since it will now be purchasable with Emblems from the Relic vendor. Phase 3 does introduce a new Idol option, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47668/idol-of-mutilation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Mutilation</span></a>, which provides benefits both in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=768/cat-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_catform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cat Form</span></a> and in <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=9634/dire-bear-form">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_racial_bearform.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dire Bear Form</span></a>, but the new Idol is unfortunately strictly worse than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45509/idol-of-the-corruptor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Corruptor</span></a> for boss tanking. Not only is the uptime of its <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67354/evasion">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_blessingofagility.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Evasion</span></a> proc much lower than the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=64951/primal-wrath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_blessingofagility.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primal Wrath</span></a> proc from <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45509/idol-of-the-corruptor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Corruptor</span></a> due to the 8 second internal cooldown on the former, but the <i>value</i> of the proc buff is also substantially lower, since 162 Agility is 45% better for tank survivability than 200 Dodge Rating based on simulation comparisons.<br/>
<br/>The only scenario where <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47668/idol-of-mutilation">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Mutilation</span></a> will outperform <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45509/idol-of-the-corruptor">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qirajidol_strife.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of the Corruptor</span></a> for bear tanking is on trash, since <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48564/mangle-bear">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_druid_mangle2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mangle (Bear)</span></a> is hardly ever cast on AoE packs. However, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=38365/idol-of-perspicacious-attacks">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/classic_ability_druid_demoralizingroar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Idol of Perspicacious Attacks</span></a> will be even better in that context, since trash mobs rarely hit hard enough to prioritize avoidance over more <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48562/swipe-bear">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_monsterclaw_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Swipe (Bear)</span></a> damage.<div class="pad"></div>
